per's. Like the paper, it does not require Σp_k = 1. The law of G: gumbelInputs is the product of gumbelLaw, the push-forward of Exp(1) under −log, so the G_k are i.i.d. standard Gumbel. μ^τ: when every p_k>0, softmaxWeights equals eq:gumbel coordinate by coordinate, and the law is taken on L1Vec n with the 1-norm W. μ^0: hardWeights is the one-hot vector at the first argmax of log p_k + G_k. Off the null set where two scores tie, this equals the almost-sure limit as τ↓0 under the same G, so its law is μ^0 as pinned in ass:pin-165. Both maps are measurable, so neither law collapses to 0. Bound: 2(n−1)τ − 2n(n−1)e^{-1}τ·log τ, with (n−1 : ℕ) exact because n ≥ 1. The value is positive because log τ < 0, so ENNReal.ofReal loses nothing. ass:pin-2 (the event E_δ) is used only in the proof, not in the statement."}],"assumption_verdicts":[],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":null}

