osen density version, which matches the standard convention for objects defined up to null sets. The scalar-treatment side condition (`valueDim` = 1, treatment = `scalarNode` T) is presupposed by t ∈ [t1,t2] ⊂ ℝ. Equivalent in both directions."},{"obj_id":"ass:prop-lip-ate-no-confounding","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"G is the bidirected-arrow graph of `CanonicalSCM` kind dims dag G C (its C²-components are the maximal G-cliques), and the consumer prop:lip-ate passes exactly that G. So ∀ i j, ¬G.Adj i j says the causal graph has no bidirected arrows, which is the paper's 'no hidden confounder in 𝒢'. `SimpleGraph` is irreflexive, so self-pairs carry no content. Equivalent."},{"obj_id":"ass:prop-convg-opt-setting","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"Here M is a `MetricSpace` (variable binder at Auxiliary.lean:23). (1) Θ n ⊆ Θ(n+1) ⊆ ThetaInf, with ThetaInf = closure(⋃ n, Θ n), gives the nested chain inside Θ_∞. (2) ε and δ are positive. (3) ε, δ and τ all tend to 0. (4) `ContinuousOn` f and `ContinuousOn` (gn n) on ThetaInf is the same as continuity of the restrictions to Θ_∞, and functions on M are a conservative extension of functions on Θ_∞. Lean indexes from 0 where the paper starts at 1. Shifting every sequence by one index converts each side to the other and preserves every clause, so the two are equivalent."}],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":null}

