{"statement_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"def:definition-2","verdict":"matched","note":"IsC2Component G C := Maximal G.IsClique C, where G : SimpleGraph (Fin n) is the bidirected part of the causal graph (the same SimpleGraph-valued component that causalGraph builds via fromRel). G.IsClique C says distinct vertices of C are pairwise adjacent, i.e. joined by a bidirected arrow; Maximal is maximality under ⊆. This is exactly pin-177 ('inclusion maximal among subsets whose distinct vertices are pairwise joined by a bidirected arrow'). Self-arrows (pin-94) do not matter, because cliques only constrain distinct vertices. Equal extension in both directions."},{"obj_id":"def:definition-3","verdict":"matched","note":"Unfolded: (1) uniformLatents makes the latent law the product of uniform laws on [0,1]^{dims j} (volume restricted to Icc 0 1, coordinatewise) and iid standard Gumbels (gumbelLaw = Exp(1) pushed forward by -log), all mutually independent, as pins 161, 10 and 84 require. Block dimensions may vary by j; the paper's own generator architectures use varying cube dimensions (pins 162 and fix-676b96c3), so 'i.i.d.' means independent uniform-cube blocks. (2) For continuous nodes, propensity = continuousMap on the domain. For categorical nodes, propensity is nonnegative with positive sum on the structural input domain (pins 156 and fix-c0174608), and the label equals the first argmax of extendedLog(weight) + g, with log 0 = ⊥ (pins fix-c356d336 and 156). That equality holds for every admissible input and almost every g. Since G_{V_i} is read only by V_i and is independent of everything else, Fubini makes this an almost-sure identity of V_i under every intervention, so all laws agree with the exact argmax model. (3) structuralNetworks makes every continuous map and every propensity map equal, on the domain, to a ReLUNet of some width W and depth L, up to an input reindexing (the NN class is invariant under permuting inputs), as pins 161, 118 and owner-3 require. The propensity field is a conservative extension: every paper NCM expands by taking propensity = its network f_i, and every expansion forgets to a paper NCM. Equal extension."},{"obj_id":"def:definition-4","verdict":"matched","note":"ate = ∫ outcomeContrast dM.latentLaw, where outcomeContrast(u) = Y(intervenedEval t u) − Y(intervenedEval t₀ u) for a scalar coordinate of Y. This is E_{u~P(U)}[Y(t) − Y(t₀)]. The side conditions only make the paper's domain explicit: valueDim(kind Y) = 1 because the ATE is a scalar contrast; sameTreatment because both t and t₀ are values of the same treatment set T; integrability of the contrast because the real expectation presupposes it (it is also implied by the K-boundedness pins 168 and 154). LawIntervention admissibility only requires categorical treatment values to be valid labels. Equivalent on the stated domain."},{"obj_id":"def:eq-structure-equation","verdict":"matched","note":"Latents: component, exhaustive and distinct make C a bijective enumeration of exactly the C²-components of G. blockLaw gives arbitrary probability laws for U_C, degenerate ones included (pin-owner-1). CanonicalSCM.latentLaw is the product of the block laws with iid standard Gumbels, n_i of them per categorical node (noiseDim), so the family is mutually independent (pins 178 and 10). Equations: f_i reads exactly Pa(V_i) and {U_C : V_i ∈ C} through incidence {j | i ∈ C j}. canonicalMechanism gives V_i = f_i for continuous nodes and the first argmax of g_k + extendedLog(f_i)_k for categorical nodes, with log 0 = ⊥ and a fixed measurable tie rule (pins 178 and 156). simplex puts f_i(x) in Δ_{n_i} at every admissible structural input, which is pin-178's 'every structural input'. categoricalPositive (n_i > 0) is presupposed by [n_i] and Δ_{n_i}. Measurability is regularity bookkeeping. Values of the ambient f off the admissible inputs are a conservative extension: evalSteps only evaluates admissible inputs, because categorical parents and interventions carry label+1 values,