ricalWeightsPositiveOn M p none`) requires, for every categorical node and every structural input in the domain, nonnegative weights with positive total. That is the nonnegative weight vector with a well-defined ‖f_i(x)‖_1, and for nonnegative weights Σ_l p_l = ‖p‖_1. `categoricalConditionalLaw` states p_j(x)/Σ_l p_l(x) = E[1{label = j} | σ(structuralInputRV)] a.e. Here the label is M.f at input x = (Pa(V_i), U_{V_i}) with that node's categorical noise, i.e. V_i. So this is P(V_i = j | x) = (f_i(x))_j/‖f_i(x)‖_1, read a.e. as the standard convention for conditional probabilities. `extendedLog 0 = ⊥` records log 0 = −∞. That convention is the one the Gumbel-argmax mechanism uses through `firstArgmax (extendedLog w_j + g_j)` (Setup/Networks.lean:289-292), so zero coordinates never win the argmax. This is consistent with the binding ruling on tie completion (ass:bk-owner-8)."}],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":{"kind":"scaffold-mismatch","obj_id":"ass:pin-fix-f66ad243","reason":"DepthExpressionConvention compares depth as n → ∞ against the constant function 1+log din, so its dependence on din is vacuous (it reduces to Θ(1)). The frozen pin means depth is Θ(1+log d_in) as a function of d_in with fixed constant factors (d_in = 1 giving Θ(1)), which is how thm:consistency realizes it with c0·⌈1+log d_in⌉. Restate the predicate as a dimension-uniform two-sided bound c₁(1+log d) ≤ depth d ≤ c₂(1+log d) for all d ≥ 1.","unpinned":"","witness":null}}

